      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A method of classification of outbred albino rats by means of forced swimming in a tank filled with water and equipped by freely turning wheels was developed. Using this technique a population of albino rats can be divided into three groups: highly active (HA), low active (LA) animals, and rats with intermediate activity. HA animals exhibit stable behaviour in forced swimming and conflict situation paradigms. They are also more sensitive to a benzodiazepine anxiolytic phenazepam in conflict situation test. At the same time, LA rats decrease their activity and are less sensitive to phenazepam. Both groups (LA and HA) are not homogeneous: each of them includes animals demonstrating quite another type of behaviour compared with a majority of rats."},
